    "patronages": "St. Agatha of Sicily is especially invoked by people whose lives touch breast cancer patients, volcanoes, and Catania. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple February 5 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Agatha of Sicily's charity. If St. Agatha of Sicily is your confirmation name, February 5 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
