    "patronages": "St. Apollonia is especially invoked by people whose lives touch dentists, toothache sufferers, and Alexandria. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple February 9 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Apollonia's charity. If St. Apollonia is your confirmation name, February 9 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
