    "patronages": "Sts. Cyril and Methodius is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Slavic peoples, Europe, and translators. Patronage names a friendship in heaven, not a superstition that bypasses the Cross. A simple February 14 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors Sts. Cyril's charity. Parishes named for Sts. Cyril can treat this date as a soft “patronal day” even when it is only a memorial.",
    "legacy": "The lasting imprint of Sts. Cyril is pastoral: a finished race that now encourages others still on the road. Parents can treat February 14 as a micro-feast: one story, one prayer, one act of kindness. Guide Catholic keeps this profile online so English-speaking Catholics can find Sts. Cyril quickly when February 14 arrives — or when a need connected to Slavic peoples, Europe, and translators suddenly becomes personal.",
