    "patronages": "St. Patrick is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Ireland, engineers, and snake bites. Patronage names a friendship in heaven, not a superstition that bypasses the Cross. A simple March 17 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Patrick's charity. Parishes named for St. Patrick can treat this date as a soft “patronal day” even when it is only a memorial.",
