    "patronages": "St. Peter Chanel is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Oceania, Marist missionaries, and Wallis and Futuna. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple April 28 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Peter Chanel's charity. If St. Peter Chanel is your confirmation name, April 28 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
