    "patronages": "St. Ignatius of Laconi is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Capuchins, Sardinia, and beggars. Patronage names a friendship in heaven, not a superstition that bypasses the Cross. A simple May 11 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Ignatius of Laconi's charity. Parishes named for St. Ignatius of Laconi can treat this date as a soft “patronal day” even when it is only a memorial.",
