    "patronages": "Sts. Marcellinus and Peter is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Rome, stonecutters, and early martyrs. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple June 2 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors Sts. Marcellinus's charity. If Sts. Marcellinus is your confirmation name, June 2 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
