    "patronages": "St. Bonaventure is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Bologna, theologians, and Franciscans. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple July 15 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Bonaventure's charity. If St. Bonaventure is your confirmation name, July 15 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
    "legacy": "St. Bonaventure survives in missals, church titles, and art because concrete holiness still draws people tired of cynicism. Homilists who name St. Bonaventure when the calendar aligns give the faithful a person, not only a principle. Guide Catholic keeps this profile online so English-speaking Catholics can find St. Bonaventure quickly when July 15 arrives — or when a need connected to Bologna, theologians, and Franciscans suddenly becomes personal.",
    "howToHonorToday": "If your schedule allows, attend Mass on July 15; even a quiet weekday memorial joins you to the universal Church remembering St. Bonaventure. At home, read one short paragraph about St. Bonaventure and pray for someone whose struggle relates to Bologna, theologians, and Franciscans. Add one concrete deed: a donation, a visit, a decade of the Rosary, or a message of reconciliation offered in St. Bonaventure's spirit. If church is impossible that day, read St. Bonaventure in the Roman Martyrology or a trusted Catholic reference, then make an act of spiritual communion and return to the sacraments when you can.",
