    "patronages": "St. Christina the Astonishing is especially invoked by people whose lives touch mental health, millers, and Belgium. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple July 24 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Christina the Astonishing's charity. If St. Christina the Astonishing is your confirmation name, July 24 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
    "legacy": "St. Christina the Astonishing survives in missals, church titles, and art because concrete holiness still draws people tired of cynicism. Homilists who name St. Christina the Astonishing when the calendar aligns give the faithful a person, not only a principle. Guide Catholic keeps this profile online so English-speaking Catholics can find St. Christina the Astonishing quickly when July 24 arrives — or when a need connected to mental health, millers, and Belgium suddenly becomes personal.",
