    "historicalContext": "Parish bulletins usually list extra Masses or blessings when August 15 carries solemn weight. In the United States, if diocesan law makes the date a Holy Day of Obligation, planning travel around Mass becomes part of the witness. Arrive a few minutes early: silence before the opening hymn is often the difference between “checking a box” and receiving the feast.",
