    "patronages": "St. Thérèse of Lisieux is especially invoked by people whose lives touch missions, florists, pilots, and Russia. Catholic teaching is clear: saints intercede; they do not replace the mediation of Christ. A simple October 1 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Thérèse of Lisieux's charity. If St. Thérèse of Lisieux is your confirmation name, October 1 is a yearly checkup on the promises that name implies.",
