    "howToHonorToday": "If your schedule allows, attend Mass on October 1; even a quiet weekday memorial joins you to the universal Church remembering St. Thérèse of Lisieux. At home, read one short paragraph about St. Thérèse of Lisieux and pray for someone whose struggle relates to missions, florists, pilots, and Russia. Add one concrete deed: a donation, a visit, a decade of the Rosary, or a message of reconciliation offered in St. Thérèse of Lisieux's spirit. If church is impossible that day, read St. Thérèse of Lisieux in the Roman Martyrology or a trusted Catholic reference, then make an act of spiritual communion and return to the sacraments when you can.",
