    "patronages": "St. Elizabeth of the Trinity is especially invoked by people whose lives touch Carmelites, contemplatives, and spiritual writers. Patronage names a friendship in heaven, not a superstition that bypasses the Cross. A simple November 5 practice: name one intention aloud, pray an Our Father and Hail Mary, then do one work of mercy that mirrors St. Elizabeth of the Trinity's charity. Parishes named for St. Elizabeth of the Trinity can treat this date as a soft “patronal day” even when it is only a memorial.",
