    "howToHonorToday": "Make Mass the centerpiece of December 31 when possible — the Eucharist is how Catholics most fittingly honor St. Sylvester I. At home, read one short paragraph about St. Sylvester I and pray for someone whose struggle relates to New Year's Eve, Rome, popes, and donkeys. Choose a single act that St. Sylvester I would recognize — mercy toward the poor, defense of truth, or hidden fidelity. If church is impossible that day, read St. Sylvester I in the Roman Martyrology or a trusted Catholic reference, then make an act of spiritual communion and return to the sacraments when you can.",
